diff --git a/docs/parameters.md b/docs/parameters.md
index 58f3219..b7159c9 100644
--- a/docs/parameters.md
+++ b/docs/parameters.md
@@ -53,3 +53,11 @@ The option's names are `-t` and `--times`. More names are available for options
 
     invoke(multi_echo, ['--times=3', 'index.txt'], prog_name='multi_echo')
 ```
+
+(parameter-spec)=
+
+### Spec
+
+{attr}`Parameter.spec` is how the user spells a parameter on the command line. Click uses it to name the parameter in messages. For an option, it is the longest prefixed declaration among its primary names, so `-t, --times` gives `--times`, `--color/--no-color` gives `--color`, and `/debug;/no-debug` gives `/debug`. An explicit name such as `count` in `-t, --times, count` never appears in the spec. For an argument, it is the metavar if one is given, or the name in upper case, so `filename` gives `FILENAME` and `metavar="SRC"` gives `SRC`. Unlike the metavar in usage, the spec has no `[]`, `...`, or `!`.
+
+Earlier versions exposed this as `Parameter.human_readable_name`. That property is deprecated as of 8.6.0 and will be removed in Click 9.0. It returns the spec. Override `spec` rather than `human_readable_name` in a custom {class}`Parameter` subclass.
