+- Messages that name a parameter use its spec, the way it is spelled on the command line. A deprecated option reports `'--my-option'` rather than `'my_option'`, and a missing option reports `Missing parameter: -a` rather than `a`. `Option.get_help_spec()` moved to `Parameter.get_help_spec()` and returns the spec, such as `--times`, rather than the option's full help column. Use `Option.get_help_record()` for the full column. A subclass that overrode `Option.get_help_spec()` to change the help column no longer changes help output; override `get_help_record()` instead. An argument's `get_help_spec()` returns its metavar, such as `[FILENAME]...`.
 
